            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SHARONANNH"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious and decadent. Used Godiva in place of the vodka, maraschino juice in lieu of grenadine, and lined the glass with the syrup instead of mixing it in. It tastes so much like a chocolate covered cherry that I'm deliciously happy. Thank you for a wonderful concoction.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-09T18:13:44.353Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Terri Tuttle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it! I could not find chocolate vodka, so I used Godiva chocolate liqueur. Absolutely delicious! Definite on to keep on hand. I added a photo, but I had already drank some (couldn’t wait haha)!",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-31T03:37:52.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lovestohost"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was easy to throw together after a long Friday (once I procured the ingredients, which aren’t staples in our bar). I subbed a splash of cherry juice for grenadine and oat milk for half and half with no ill effects. I’ve no clue how to garnish with a hard Hershey kiss, though (mine is in the bottom of my glass). Perfect for chocolate cherry lovers, with a boozy kick. Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-05T22:22:37.463Z"
          },
          {
